#NEXUS

[ d'emic2012b_fig5: Sauropod cladogram drawn as a slanted tree, 28 tips. Two trichotomies, drawn as three lines meeting at one point: Abydosaurus + Cedarosaurus + Venenosaurus, and Euhelopus + Daxiatitan + (Tangvayosaurus, Phuwiangosaurus). Europasaurus and Qiaowanlong run straight through the circles of Brachiosauridae and Euhelopodidae: each is the first-branching member of that clade. Chubutisaurus joins the backbone just below the Titanosauria circle, outside it. Joins along the backbone were checked by measuring each 45-degree line where it crosses rows of the image. Random-sample case (seed 20261106); topology only. ]

BEGIN TAXA;
    DIMENSIONS NTAX=28;
    TAXLABELS
        Shunosaurus
        Omeisaurus
        Jobaria
        Atlasaurus
        Diplodocoidea
        Camarasaurus
        Tehuelchesaurus
        Europasaurus
        Giraffatitan
        Brachiosaurus
        Abydosaurus
        Cedarosaurus
        Venenosaurus
        Ligabuesaurus
        Sauroposeidon
        Tastavinsaurus
        Qiaowanlong
        Erketu
        Euhelopus
        Daxiatitan
        Tangvayosaurus
        Phuwiangosaurus
        Chubutisaurus
        Andesaurus
        Malawisaurus
        Opisthocoelicaudia
        Saltasaurini
        Alamosaurus
    ;
END;

BEGIN TREES;
    TREE d'emic2012b_fig5 = [&R] (Shunosaurus,(Omeisaurus,(Jobaria,(Atlasaurus,(Diplodocoidea,(Camarasaurus,(Tehuelchesaurus,((Europasaurus,(Giraffatitan,(Brachiosaurus,(Abydosaurus,Cedarosaurus,Venenosaurus)))),(Ligabuesaurus,(Sauroposeidon,(Tastavinsaurus,((Qiaowanlong,(Erketu,(Euhelopus,Daxiatitan,(Tangvayosaurus,Phuwiangosaurus)))),(Chubutisaurus,(Andesaurus,(Malawisaurus,(Opisthocoelicaudia,(Saltasaurini,Alamosaurus)))))))))))))))));
END;
